 "post": {
  "title": "Why You Look Better in a Group Photo #shorts",
  "description": "Lila hates her solo selfie but loves the group photo with Mae, same face, same day. Drew Walker & Edward Vul (UC San Diego) tested this in Psychological Science (online 2013, print 2014): across five experiments with over 130 undergraduates, the same person was rated more attractive in a group photo than cropped alone, and in collages of 4, 9 and 16 faces too. Their explanation: we average the faces in a group, each face looks more average, and average faces look more attractive. Honest caveat: the boost is small, about the 49th to the 51st percentile (\"definitely small\", Vul). The cheerleader effect. #psychology #shorts #selfie #groupphoto",
  "tags": [
